    ## Nothing; the receiver is rewritten. Use `get_removeprefix` for the pure
    ## form that returns a new `string`.
    ##
    ## ## Memoria
    ## The old buffer is released; nothing is left for the caller to
    ## banish.
    ##
    ## ## Ejemplo
    ## ```pengu
    ## var s as string is "abc"
    ## calling s.removeprefix with "-"
    ## ```
    weave removeprefix with prefix as string into void:
        var old as string is essence of self
        let new_s as string is calling self.get_removeprefix with prefix
        banish old
        set essence of self is new_s

    ## In-place form of `get_removesuffix`: computes the new text and installs it
    ## in the receiver, releasing the buffer it replaces.
    ##
    ## ## Retorno
    ## Nothing; the receiver is rewritten. Use `get_removesuffix` for the pure
    ## form that returns a new `string`.
    ##
    ## ## Memoria
    ## The old buffer is released; nothing is left for the caller to
    ## banish.
    ##
    ## ## Ejemplo
    ## ```pengu
    ## var s as string is "abc"
    ## calling s.removesuffix with "-"
    ## ```
    weave removesuffix with suffix as string into void:
        var old as string is essence of self
        let new_s as string is calling self.get_removesuffix with suffix
        banish old
        set essence of self is new_s

    ## In-place form of `get_truncate`: computes the new text and installs it
    ## in the receiver, releasing the buffer it replaces.
    ##
    ## ## Retorno
    ## Nothing; the receiver is rewritten. Use `get_truncate` for the pure
    ## form that returns a new `string`.
    ##
    ## ## Memoria
    ## The old buffer is released; nothing is left for the caller to
    ## banish.
    ##
    ## ## Ejemplo
    ## ```pengu
    ## var s as string is "abc"
    ## calling s.truncate with 0, "-"
    ## ```
    weave truncate with max_len as int, suffix as string into void:
        var old as string is essence of self
        let new_s as string is calling self.get_truncate with max_len, suffix
        banish old
        set essence of self is new_s

    ## In-place form of `get_ellipsis`: computes the new text and installs it
    ## in the receiver, releasing the buffer it replaces.
    ##
    ## ## Retorno
    ## Nothing; the receiver is rewritten. Use `get_ellipsis` for the pure
    ## form that returns a new `string`.
    ##
    ## ## Memoria
    ## The old buffer is released; nothing is left for the caller to
    ## banish.
    ##
    ## ## Ejemplo
    ## ```pengu
    ## var s as string is "abc"
    ## calling s.ellipsis with 0
    ## ```
    weave ellipsis with max_len as int into void:
        var old as string is essence of self
        let new_s as string is calling self.get_ellipsis with max_len
        banish old
        set essence of self is new_s

# --- Module functions ---------------------------------------------------
# Functional form of every method: the receiver becomes the first parameter `s`
# and the `weave` delegates to the method of the same name, documented above.
# The contract and the edge cases are identical.

## Functional form of `len`: number of bytes in `s`.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `s`: the string to measure.
##
## ## Retorno
## The byte length as an `int`.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## calling scrolls.len with "abc"    # 3
## ```
weave len with s as string into int:
    return calling s.len
## Functional form of `is_empty`: true when `s` has zero bytes.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `s`: the string to test.
##
## ## Retorno
## `true` for "" and `false` otherwise.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## calling scrolls.is_empty with ""    # true
## ```
weave is_empty with s as string into bool:
    return calling s.is_empty

# --- Search -------------------------------------------------------------
## Functional form of `contains`: true when `sub` occurs in `s`.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `s`: the haystack.
## - `sub`: the needle; may be empty.
##
## ## Retorno
## `true` when `sub` is found.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## calling scrolls.contains with "abc", "b"    # true
## ```
weave contains with s as string, sub as string into bool:
    return calling s.contains with sub
## Functional form of `starts_with`: true when `s` starts with `prefix`.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `s`: the string to test.
## - `prefix`: the prefix; empty always matches.
##
## ## Retorno
## `true` when the prefix matches.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## calling scrolls.starts_with with "abc", "ab"    # true
## ```
weave starts_with with s as string, prefix as string into bool:
    return calling s.starts_with with prefix
## Functional form of `starts_with_any`: true when any prefix matches.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `s`: the string to test.
## - `prefixes`: the candidate prefixes; empty never matches.
##
## ## Retorno
## `true` at the first match, `false` otherwise.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## calling scrolls.starts_with_any with "abc", ["x", "ab"]    # true
## ```
weave starts_with_any with s as string, prefixes as list of string into bool:
    return calling s.starts_with_any with prefixes
## Functional form of `ends_with`: true when `s` ends with `suffix`.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `s`: the string to test.
## - `suffix`: the suffix; empty always matches.
##
## ## Retorno
## `true` when the suffix matches.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## calling scrolls.ends_with with "abc", "bc"    # true
## ```
weave ends_with with s as string, suffix as string into bool:
    return calling s.ends_with with suffix
## Functional form of `ends_with_any`: true when any suffix matches.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `s`: the string to test.
## - `suffixes`: the candidate suffixes; empty never matches.
##
## ## Retorno
## `true` at the first match, `false` otherwise.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## calling scrolls.ends_with_any with "abc", ["x", "bc"]    # true
## ```
weave ends_with_any with s as string, suffixes as list of string into bool:
    return calling s.ends_with_any with suffixes
## Functional form of `index_of`: first index of `sub`, or -1.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `s`: the haystack.
## - `sub`: the needle; may be empty.
##
## ## Retorno
## The 0-based byte index, or -1.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## calling scrolls.index_of with "abc", "c"    # 2
## ```
weave index_of with s as string, sub as string into int:
    return calling s.index_of with sub
## Functional form of `last_index_of`: last index of `sub`, or -1.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `s`: the haystack.
## - `sub`: the needle; may be empty.
##
## ## Retorno
## The 0-based byte index of the last match, or -1.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## calling scrolls.last_index_of with "abca", "a"    # 3
## ```
weave last_index_of with s as string, sub as string into int:
    return calling s.last_index_of with sub

# --- Slicing ------------------------------------------------------------
## Functional form of `substring`: bytes from `start_pos` to `end_pos`.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `s`: the source string.
## - `start_pos`: first byte index to keep.
## - `end_pos`: byte index to stop at.
##
## ## Retorno
## A new owned string; release it with `banish`.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## calling scrolls.substring with "abcdef", 1, 3    # "bc"
## ```
weave substring with s as string, start_pos as int, end_pos as int into string:
    return calling s.get_substring with start_pos, end_pos
## Functional form of `char_at`: the byte at `idx` as a one-byte string.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `s`: the source string.
## - `idx`: the byte position.
##
## ## Retorno
## A new owned one-byte string; release it with `banish`.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## calling scrolls.char_at with "abc", 1    # "b"
## ```
weave char_at with s as string, idx as int into string:
    return calling s.get_char_at with idx

# --- Case ---------------------------------------------------------------
## Functional form of `lower`: ASCII A-Z lowered.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `s`: the string to transform.
##
## ## Retorno
## A new owned string; release it with `banish`.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## calling scrolls.lower with "Ab"    # "ab"
## ```
weave lower with s as string into string:
    return calling s.get_lower
## Functional form of `upper`: ASCII a-z uppercased.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `s`: the string to transform.
##
## ## Retorno
## A new owned string; release it with `banish`.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## calling scrolls.upper with "Ab"    # "AB"
## ```
weave upper with s as string into string:
    return calling s.get_upper
## @deprecated Use lower instead.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `s`: the string to transform.
##
## ## Retorno
## Same as `lower`; kept only for compatibility.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## calling scrolls.to_lower with "AbC"    # "abc"
## ```
weave to_lower with s as string into string:
    return calling s.get_to_lower
## @deprecated Use upper instead.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `s`: the string to transform.
##
## ## Retorno
## Same as `upper`; kept only for compatibility.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## calling scrolls.to_upper with "AbC"    # "ABC"
## ```
weave to_upper with s as string into string:
    return calling s.get_to_upper

# --- Whitespace ---------------------------------------------------------
## Functional form of `trim`: strip whitespace from both ends.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `s`: the string to trim.
##
## ## Retorno
## A new owned string; release it with `banish`.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## calling scrolls.trim with "  a  "    # "a"
## ```
weave trim with s as string into string:
    return calling s.get_trim
## Functional form of `strip`: alias of `trim`.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `s`: the string to trim.
##
## ## Retorno
## A new owned string; release it with `banish`.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## calling scrolls.strip with "  a  "    # "a"
## ```
weave strip with s as string into string:
    return calling s.get_strip
## Functional form of `trim_start`: strip leading whitespace.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `s`: the string to trim.
##
## ## Retorno
## A new owned string; release it with `banish`.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## calling scrolls.trim_start with " a"    # "a"
## ```
weave trim_start with s as string into string:
    return calling s.get_trim_start
## Functional form of `trim_end`: strip trailing whitespace.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `s`: the string to trim.
##
## ## Retorno
## A new owned string; release it with `banish`.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## calling scrolls.trim_end with "a "    # "a"
## ```
weave trim_end with s as string into string:
    return calling s.get_trim_end

# --- Replacing and splitting --------------------------------------------
## Functional form of `replace`: replace the first occurrence.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `s`: the source string.
## - `from_str`: the text to replace.
## - `to_str`: the replacement text.
##
## ## Retorno
## A new owned string; release it with `banish`.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## calling scrolls.replace with "abc", "b", "X"    # "aXc"
## ```
weave replace with s as string, from_str as string, to_str as string into string:
    return calling s.get_replace with from_str, to_str
## Functional form of `replace_all`: replace every non-overlapping occurrence.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `s`: the source string.
## - `from_str`: the text to replace; empty changes nothing.
## - `to_str`: the replacement text.
##
## ## Retorno
## A new owned string; release it with `banish`.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## calling scrolls.replace_all with "aaa", "a", "b"    # "bbb"
## ```
weave replace_all with s as string, from_str as string, to_str as string into string:
    return calling s.get_replace_all with from_str, to_str
## Functional form of `split`: split on every delimiter.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `s`: the source string.
## - `delim`: the separator; empty keeps the whole string.
##
## ## Retorno
## A new owned `list of string`; release it with `banish`.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## calling scrolls.split with "a,b", ","    # ["a", "b"]
## ```
weave split with s as string, delim as string into list of string:
    return calling s.split with delim
## Functional form of `splitn`: split into at most `n` parts.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `s`: the source string.
## - `delim`: the separator; empty keeps the whole string.
## - `n`: maximum number of parts; `n <= 0` performs no split.
##
## ## Retorno
## A new owned `list of string`; release it with `banish`.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## calling scrolls.splitn with "a,b,c", ",", 2    # ["a", "b,c"]
## ```
weave splitn with s as string, delim as string, n as int into list of string:
    return calling s.splitn with delim, n
## Functional form of `rsplit`: split scanning from the right.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `s`: the source string.
## - `delim`: the separator; empty keeps the whole string.
##
## ## Retorno
## A new owned `list of string` in left-to-right order; release it with `banish`.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## calling scrolls.rsplit with "a:b:c", ":"    # ["a", "b", "c"]
## ```
weave rsplit with s as string, delim as string into list of string:
    return calling s.rsplit with delim
## Functional form of `repeat`: repeat `s` `count` times.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `s`: the string to repeat.
## - `count`: the number of copies.
##
## ## Retorno
## A new owned string; `count <= 0` or empty `s` yields "". Release it with
## `banish`.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## calling scrolls.repeat with "ab", 2    # "abab"
## ```
weave repeat with s as string, count as int into string:
    return calling s.get_repeat with count
## Functional form of `repeat_join`: repeat `s` and join with `sep`.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `s`: the string to repeat.
## - `count`: the number of copies.
## - `sep`: the text placed between copies.
##
## ## Retorno
## A new owned string; `count <= 0` or empty `s` yields "". Release it with
## `banish`.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## calling scrolls.repeat_join with "ab", 2, "-"    # "ab-ab"
## ```
weave repeat_join with s as string, count as int, sep as string into string:
    return calling s.get_repeat_join with count, sep
## Functional form of `reverse`: bytes in reverse order.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `s`: the string to reverse.
##
## ## Retorno
## A new owned string; release it with `banish`.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## calling scrolls.reverse with "abc"    # "cba"
## ```
weave reverse with s as string into string:
    return calling s.get_reverse
## Functional form of `is_alpha`: true for one or more ASCII letters.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `s`: the string to classify.
##
## ## Retorno
## `true` only for `[A-Za-z]+`.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## calling scrolls.is_alpha with "aB"    # true
## ```
weave is_alpha with s as string into bool:
    return calling s.is_alpha
## Functional form of `is_digit`: true for one or more ASCII digits.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `s`: the string to classify.
##
## ## Retorno
## `true` only for `[0-9]+`.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## calling scrolls.is_digit with "12"    # true
## ```
weave is_digit with s as string into bool:
    return calling s.is_digit
## Functional form of `is_alnum`: true for one or more ASCII letters or digits.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `s`: the string to classify.
##
## ## Retorno
## `true` only for `[A-Za-z0-9]+`.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## calling scrolls.is_alnum with "a1"    # true
## ```
weave is_alnum with s as string into bool:
    return calling s.is_alnum
## Functional form of `capitalize`: first letter upper, rest lower.
##
## ## Parámetros
## - `s`: the string to capitalize.
##
## ## Retorno
## A new owned string; "" stays "".
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
